{
  "id": 28,
  "Specification": "c1cs: A crash-fault-tolerant consensus protocol for N processes with at most F crash failures and T Byzantine failures (assumption: 3*T < N). Processes broadcast proposed values, collect N-T proposal messages, then decide based on threshold conditions. Actions: Crash, Receive, Propose, Core_T1 (two-branch decision logic using CHOOSE), T2 (decide upon receiving a Decision message), DoNothing. Properties: TypeOK, Validity (decided value equals some process's initial value), Agreement (all non-bottom decided values agree, with CALL-DONE consistency), WeakAgreement, Termination (eventually all processes reach CRASH/DONE/CALL), IndStrengthens (inductive invariant strengthening).",
